  "body": "Part of #2607 (slice S1 of 6).\n\nThe order of the maintainer (2026-11-18): \"GPU shader issues get priority\". The umbrella quotes: \"Add a GPU shader issue and that is for voxel simulation..\".\n\n## What\nAdd a CPU reference for the future GPU removal kernel, in `camcraft-sim`. No GPU code.\n\n1. A per-cell cut function in f32 that has the same arithmetic as the WGSL kernel of S2:\n   - tile-relative coordinates;\n   - ball and upright flat end mills on linear moves only;\n   - the order-preserving f32-to-u32 map and the max law.\n2. A brick work list: from a batch of moves, the list of bricks and cells that each move window touches. Use the windows of `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/field_cut.rs` and `field_batch.rs`.\n3. Output in the dense lattice layout of `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/preview/pack.rs` (`pack_cut`).\n4. Any other tool kind refuses by name. It does not cut in a different way.\n\n## Tests (CPU reference test)\n- One-sided parity against the f64 `field_cut` result on the same moves:\n  - f32 cut <= f64 cut + margin (never more removal);\n  - f32 cut >= f64 cut - k * eps.\n- The u32 map keeps the order for negative, zero and positive values.\n- The batch result does not change with the move order (bit equal).\n- Degenerate input (zero-length move, zero radius, NaN) refuses with a clean error.\n\n## Notes\n- Safety floor: stock simulation is `effort:high` or more.\n- No new crate edge. No decision entry is necessary.\n- This slice is display reference only. The verdict does not read it.\n\nDone means: the f32 twin and the work list are in `camcraft-sim`, with the parity, order and refusal tests green in the quick gate.\n",
